{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.KeystoneBridgeC1Binding","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.KeystoneBridgeC1Binding","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction","lean:module:QOU.Mass.BindingGevreyHalf"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KeystoneBridgeC1Binding.keystone_bridge_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KeystoneBridgeC1Binding.keystone_bridge_involution","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KeystoneBridgeC1Binding.lean#L149-L166","doc":"**Concrete discharge on the involution numbers.** `involutionNumber`\nsatisfies the involution recurrence by `rfl`, so `keystone_bridge_binding_classical`\napplies verbatim: the `(n−1)!`-normalized binding OGF built from the classical\nna-Stokes period `I(n)/n` satisfies the proved depth-2 kernel. This is the\nclassical fibre of the keystone, discharged for the corpus sequence\n(`sw-classical-jet-exactness`, `BindingGevreyHalf.involutionNumber_pos`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KeystoneBridgeC1Binding.keystone_bridge_binding_qlift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KeystoneBridgeC1Binding.keystone_bridge_binding_qlift","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KeystoneBridgeC1Binding.lean#L116-L147","doc":"**Keystone bridge C1 ↔ binding (q-lift) — PROVED.**\nOver a field with non-vanishing q-integers, for any q-na-Stokes numerator `S`\nwith the q-involution recurrence `S(n+2) = S(n+1) + [n+1]_q·S(n)`, the\nq-natural binding period `p_k = S_k/[k]_q` gives `B_k = m_e·p_k`, and its\n`N_q(k) = [k−1]_q!`-normalized carrier `b_k = B_k/[k−1]_q! = m_e·S_k/[k]_q!`\nsatisfies the PROVED depth-2 q-difference kernel\n    `[n+2]_q·b_{n+2} = b_{n+1} + b_n`\n— with `c(q) = 1`, no free constant. At `q = 1` (`qint 1 k = k`) this is the\nclassical bridge above. The q-lift uses the q-natural period `S/[n]_q`; see\nthe audit for the plain-`/n` vs `/[n]_q` definitional note. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KeystoneBridgeC1Binding.keystone_bridge_binding_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KeystoneBridgeC1Binding.keystone_bridge_binding_classical","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KeystoneBridgeC1Binding.lean#L85-L114","doc":"**Keystone bridge C1 ↔ binding (classical fibre) — PROVED.**\nFor any sequence `f` with the involution recurrence\n`f(n+2) = f(n+1) + (n+1)·f(n)`, the binding period `p_k = f_k/k` gives the\nbody term `B_k = m_e·p_k`, and its `N(k)=(k−1)!`-normalized carrier\n`b_k = B_k/(k−1)! = m_e·f_k/k!` satisfies the PROVED depth-2 confluent kernel\n    `(n+2)·b_{n+2} = b_{n+1} + b_n`.\nStated on the PERIOD directly (`b_k = m_e·(f_k/k)/(k−1)!`) so the normalizer\nis explicit; indices shifted by 1 to avoid ℕ-subtraction. The constant `m_e`\ncancels — the kernel is linear homogeneous. Discharges the normalization leg;\nthe SW-prolongation-symbol identification stays conjectural. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KeystoneBridgeC1Binding.period_carrier_strip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KeystoneBridgeC1Binding.period_carrier_strip","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KeystoneBridgeC1Binding.lean#L67-L83","doc":"**The factorial strip `N(n) = (n−1)!` (classical).** The binding PERIOD at\nindex `m+1` is `p_{m+1} = f_{m+1}/(m+1)`; the C1 carrier is\n`b_{m+1} = f_{m+1}/(m+1)!`. Since `(m+1)! = (m+1)·m!` they differ by exactly\n`m! = ((m+1)−1)!`:  `p_{m+1} = b_{m+1}·m!`, i.e. `b_{m+1} = p_{m+1}/m!`.\nThis exhibits the unique fixed normalizer `N(n) = (n−1)!`\n(equivalently `n·N(n) = n!`) reconciling the period `f_n/n` with the carrier\n`f_n/n!`. Over ℚ (`m+1` and factorials are invertible — no positive-\ncharacteristic degeneration). ","signatureChunk":0}]}